  "raw_text": "300\n\nMoses Jehova ra bik taki makaban upla nani ra padin munbia.\n \n–\n \nMoses pleaded with Jehovah to forgive the people.\n \n/ Moisés\n\nle suplicó a Jehová que perdonara al\n \npueblo.\n\nBrin dauki kan witin nani lilia asla wark taki banhbia tasba ba paradais ra lakaia dukiara.\n \n–\n \n(Jehovah) was wanting them to\n\nwork happily and unitedly in order to change the earth into a paradise.\n \n/ (Jehová) quería que trabajaran felices y unidos para\n\nconvertir la tierra en un paraíso.\n\nJehova ra puram suns d\nâ\nkaia warkka tatakra nani kau\n \nblîkb\nia dukiara\n \n–\n \nPray to Jehovah to send more harvest workers\n \n/ Oren\n\na Jehová para que envíe más trabajadores de la cosecha\n\nBalac, Moab kingka ba, sibrin kan Israel uplika nani ba ai tasbaya dakbia.\n \n–\n \nBalak, the king of Moab, was scared that the\n\nIsraelites would take away his land.\n \n/ Balac, el rey de Moab, tenía miedo de que los israelitas le quitaran su tierra.\n\nJehova wan mayunra l\nâ\nka yamni\n \nkaikbia dukiara, yawan holikira kaia sa, wibia kaka, yawan klin kaia sa.\n \n–\n \nIn order for\n\nJehovah to look at our worship as good (approve of our worship), we must be holy, that is to say, it must be clean.\n \n/ Para que\n\nJehová vea nuestra adoración como buena (apruebe nuestra adoración), debemos ser santos, es decir, debe ser limpia.\n\nImperative / Imperativa\n\nA command or order.\n \nUsually, these are formed by adding an “\ns\n” after the root of the verb.\n \n/\n\nUn comando u orden. Por lo general, estos se forman\n \nagregando una \"\ns\n\" después de la raíz del verbo.\n\nExamples/Ejemplos:\n\nDis\n \n(v\n-\nimp\n \nof/de:\n \nDiaia\n)\n \n–\n \ndrink\n \n/ bebe\n\n→\n \nNaha wainka wina dis\n \n–\n \nDrink from this wine\n \n/ Bebe de este vino\n\nDauks\n \n(v-imp of/de:\n \nDaukaia\n)\n \n–\n \ndo, make\n \n/ haz\n\n→\n \nJisas baku\n \ndauks\n \n–\n \nDo like Jesus; Imitate Jesus\n \n/ Haz como Jesús; Imita a Jesús\n\nImperative\n \n–\n \nAlternate Method Including Speaker / Imperativo - Método Alternativo incluyendo orador\n\nIf the speaker is including themself\n \nas one also to obey the command, “\npi\n” is added to the root of the verb.\n \n/\n\nSi el hablante se incluye a sí mismo como alguien que también obedece el comando, se agrega \"\npi\n\" a la raíz del verbo.\n\nExample/Ejemplo:\n\nAiwanpi\n \n(v-alt-imp of/de:\n \nAiwanaia\n)\n \n–\n \n(let’s all) sing\n \n/ (vamos todos) a cantar\n\nProhibitive / Prohibitiva\n\nThe prohibitive form is formed by a\ndding “\npara\n” to the\n \nroot of the verb /\n\nLa forma prohibitiva se forma agregando \"\npara\n\" a la raíz del verbo\n\nExamples/Ejemplos:\n\nTawaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto turn, to turn around, to change direction, to return\n \n/ girar, cambiar de dirección, volver\n\n→\n \nMihtam aihkika ra tawpara\n \n–\n \nDo not turn to your right\n \n/ No gire a la derecha\n\nKupia baikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto make or cause to get angry, to infuriate, to enrage\n \n/ hacer enojar, enfurecer\n\n→\n \nKupiam baikpara\n \n–\n \nDo not become angry\n \n/ No te enfades\n\nKapara\n \n(v-proh of/de:\n \nKaia\n)\n \n–\n \ndon’t be\n \n/ no seas\n\n→\n \nSinskas kapara\n \n–\n \ndon’t be foolish\n \n/ no seas tonto",
